g></p><p><br></p><p><strong>The link will be live some 15 minutes before the advertised time; it will remain active for 7 days for you to complete watching.</strong></p><p><strong>The Cinema Club has an alternative back up stream here: </strong><a href=\\\"https://www.sandsfilms.co.uk/the-cinema-club/next-screening-watch-live.html\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\"><strong>https://www.sandsfilms.co.uk/the-cinema-club/next-screening-watch-live.html</strong></a></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Please feel free to send feedbacks, comments or complaints:</u> filmclub@sandsfilms.co.uk</strong></p>\",\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"69501805da8b11021a086b91\",\"event_bucket\":\"6161a93f49ddeb00acf3f48c\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"FREE CINEMA (in the US): Sands Films Cinema Club online presentation\",\"description\":\"<p class=\\\"ql-align-center\\\">This page is to obtain access to the broadcast of this Sands Films Cinema Club presentation</p><h1 class=\\\"ql-align-center\\\"><strong>1956: FREE CINEMA IN USA</strong></h1><p><br></p><p><strong>70 years ago,</strong>&nbsp;the Free Cinema manifesto was written to introduce a series of short films at the London’s National Film Theatre in February 1956. It was clear that the Free Cinema movement, although established to promote films “nobody would screen”, had touched on something essential.&nbsp;</p><h1 class=\\\"ql-align-center\\\">On the second evening the series presented ON THE BOWERY from Lionel Rogosin from New York.</h1>\",\"short_description\":\"1956: FREE CINEMA (in the USA)\",\"venue\":{},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-01-20T19:45:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-02-23T21:45:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"694946b284d0316a62c55fa4\",\"name\":\"Films of 1956\",\"color\":\"#08a6f1\",\"visible\":true}],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\"