chcock’s most brilliant filmmaking. Almost pure pseudo-documentary, it is absolutely objective and, simultaneously, absolutely subjective—a profound revelation of Manny’s shame, distress and fear. Throughout the film, Robert Burks’s black-and-white cinematography blends documentary realism and dreamy noirishness.</span></p>\",\"short_description\":\"Hitchcock’s most brilliant filmmaking\",\"location\":\"Sands Films Cinema\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"616324bd6f5b7b00459ce70e\",\"name\":\"Sands Films Cinema\",\"short_name\":\"Sands Cinema\",\"description\":\"Film preview theatre\",\"address\":\"82 St Marychurch Street\\nLondon, SE16 4HZ\",\"default_capacity\":null,\"color\":\"#23a833\",\"use_reserved_seating\":false,\"comscore_include\":true},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-02-03T20:00:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-02-03T22:00:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"694946b284d0316a62c55fa4\",\"name\":\"Films of 1956\",\"color\":\"#08a6f1\",\"visible\":true}],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":true,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":true,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":true,\"quantity\":63,\"ticket_buckets\":[{\"id\":\"69500c85829af45d357ca066\",\"name\":\"No charge to reserve seat, instead, please make a donation to support our work and contribute to our costs.\",\"price\":0,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":63,\"quantity_sold\":63,\"quantity_scanned\":0,\"quantity_remaining\":0,\"public\":true,\"autoissue_companion_ticket\":[],\"exclude_capacity\":false,\"lock_admin_only\":false,\"max_quantity_per_person\":3,\"variable_price\":false,\"variable_price_minimum\":0,\"variants\":[],\"applicable_pass_buckets\":[],\"is_active\":true},{\"id\":\"69500c85829af45d357ca067\",\"name\":\"\",\"price\":0,\"unlimited\":true,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"quantity_scanned\":0,\"quantity_remaining\":9007199254740991,\"public\":true,\"autoissue_companion_ticket\":[],\"exclude_capacity\":false,\"lock_admin_only\":false,\"variable_price\":false,\"variable_price_minimum\":0,\"variants\":[],\"applicable_pass_buckets\":[\"653a28fed93ee8007364add5\"],\"is_active\":true}],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6950230e706847bc8d5a84c6\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6161a93f49ddeb00acf3f48c\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"Sands Films Studio\",\"owner_id\":\"60b1303f5955f7009b7cdff3\",\"name\":\"The Wrong Man\",\"sort_key\":\"Wrong Man, The\",\"description\":\"In 1953, an innocent man named Christopher Emmanuel \\\"Manny\\\" Balestrero is arrested after being mistaken for an armed robber.\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/f92f216d4259072ef35208bb0d73d862.jpg?fit=crop&w=960&h=380\",\"poster_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/a7805d29afa16353b5f9d1489843c87a.jpg?w=300\",\"still_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/7c4c3c87c451ff7a58f705c8901ff33e.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"language\":\"Italian, English, Spanish\",\"runtime\":\"105\",\"year\":\"1956\"},\"credits\":{\"animator\":null,\"cast\":\"Henry Fonda, Vera Miles, Anthony Quayle\",\"cinematographer\":\"Robert Burks\",\"co_producer\":null,\"composer\":\"Bernard Herrmann\",\"director\":\"Alfred Hitchcock\",\"editor\":\"George Tomasini\",\"executive_producer\":null,\"filmmaker\":null,\"music\":null,\"producer\":\"Alfred Hitchcock\",\"production_design\":null,\"screenwriter\":\"Maxwell Anderson, Angus MacPhail\",\"sound_design\":null},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"imdb_id\":\"tt0051207\",\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2025-12-27T18:18:54.542Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2025-12-27T18:19:07.131Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2025-12-27T18:22:31.623Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{\"cover\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1766854269929temp-1766854269877-cover.jpg\",\"avatar\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1766854270138temp-1766854270101-avatar.jpg\"},\"custom_email_text\":\"<p>Thank you for reserving a seat at Sands Films Cinema Club.</p><p><br></p><p>Should you decide to cancel your attendance please email <a href=\\\"mailto:filmclub@sandsfilms.co.uk\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">filmclub@sandsfilms.co.uk</a></p><p>We will send you an online access instead so you can watch the film live or later at a convenient time and will make your seat available to someone else.</p><p>Thank you for your support and your donation.</p><p><br></p>\",\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[]},{\"id\":\"69501afe829af45d35807bb2\",\"event_bucket\":\"6161a93f49ddeb00acf3f48c\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"1956: THE OGRE OF ATHENS: Sands Films Cinema Club online presentation\",\"description\":\"<p class=\\\"ql-align-center\\\">This page is to obtain access to the broadcast of this Sands Films Cinema Club presentation</p><h1 class=\\\"ql-align-center\\\"><strong class=\\\"ql-size-large\\\">1956: THE OGRE OF ATHENS</strong></h1><p class=\\\"ql-align-center\\\"><strong class=\\\"ql-size-large\\\">Despite his efforts, shy and modest bank clerk Thomas struggles to fit in with the pace of modern life. On New Year’s Eve, following a series of errors, Thomas is mistaken for ‘The Ogre’, a notorious criminal who rules the streets of Athens. Suddenly, men respect him and a woman is interested in him - it’s all he’s ever wanted. However, everything comes with a price and Thomas is soon out of his depth when his white lie unravels. Rich with physical comedy and sharp social commentary, this satirical crime drama from director Nikos Koundouros (<em>Young Aphrodites</em>) is now considered to be a true classic of modern Greek cinema.</strong></p>\",\"short_description\":\"1956: THE OGRE OF ATHENS, a true classic of modern Greek cinema\",\"venue\":{},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-02-10T19:45:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-03-16T21:45:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"694946b284d0316a62c55fa4\",\"name\":\"Films of 1956\",\"color\":\"#08a6f1\",\"visible\":true}],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":true,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"trailer_url\":\"\",\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":false,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":true,\"quantity\":0,\"ticket_buckets\":[{\"id\":\"69501afe829af45d35807bb3\",\"name\":\"Watch online, Please make a donation to help us cover costs.\",\"price\":100,\"unlimited\":true,\"quantity_sold\":8,\"quantity_scanned\":0,\"quantity_remaining\":9007199254740991,\"public\":true,\"autoissue_companion_ticket\":[],\"exclude_capacity\":false,\"lock_admin_only\":false,\"max_quantity_per_person\":null,\"variable_price\":true,\"variable_price_minimum\":0,\"variants\":[],\"applicable_pass_buckets\":[],\"is_active\":true}],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"69501afe829af45d35807bb9\",\"type\":\"livestream\",\"event_bucket\":\"6161a93f49ddeb00acf3f48